M04 conversation gates: briefings stopped by a playing key conversation.
M04_Objective_Controller_JDG starts seven non-key briefings (mission start
400 -> objective 100 and prisoner markers/HUD; prison key 401 -> objective
110 and the Eva guard hint; engine room 430 -> secondary 200, pog and engine
blips; missile room 440 -> objective 300, racks pokable; first mate 410 ->
objective 600, marker 601, HUD; protect POWs 470 -> objective 800, marker
801, HUD) and M04_Start_TorpedoObjective_Zone_JDG starts the torpedo
announcement (-> custom 450 = objective 400, markers 401/402, pog). Each step
runs only from Action_Complete on ENDED. ActiveConversationClass::
Start_Conversation stops a non-key conversation with INTERRUPTED at once
while a key conversation plays (m04.ldd key: medlab guard, three missile
racks, captain key). Retail registered the monitor after Start, so that stop
was never observed and the step was lost.

Register the monitor before Start (the M10 pattern). The stop then reaches
Action_Complete synchronously; it is accepted as the briefing's end only
while a transient conversation_starting names that conversation, so
INTERRUPTED from any other source (ConversationMgrClass::Reset at level
reset/load) keeps the retail result. If Create_Conversation fails (id < 0),
the step runs directly (UNABLE_TO_INIT). Saved once-flags (unused controller
ids 49-53) make each controller step run once; the missile step keeps its
id-48 flag and the 441 fallback as a backstop; the torpedo zone is already
latched by its saved conversationPlaying. Without a key conversation Start
never touches the monitor array, so the normal path is unchanged.

Cosmetic: the controller records which torpedo was sabotaged (ids 54/55); a
450 that arrives after one torpedo was sabotaged no longer re-adds that
torpedo's radar marker, which nothing would clear. Older saves load all new
flags as false (value-initialised scripts) and keep the retail behaviour.

